 4. ⛽ Gas falls below $4 a gallon 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Data: AAA. Chart: Ben Geman/Axios Gas prices fell below $4 per gallon today for the first time since July 19, to $3.98, per AAA tracking .

 Why it matters: High prices were highly visible election-season reminders of broader cost-of-living increases that helped fuel Democratic midterm gains, Axios' Ben Geman reports. 💡 What's happening: Falling gasoline costs follow recent declines in crude oil prices.

 Traders are responding to signs of potential U.S.-Iran diplomacy and ascendant Democrats' pledges to help force an end to the conflict. Get Axios Future of Energy .

 
 
