 6. ⚡ State Department dustup in Haiti 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Photo illustration: Sarah Grillo/Axios. Photos: Saul Loeb, Marvin Recinos/AFP via Getty Images and Chip Somodevilla/Getty Images

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Axios White House reporter Marc Caputo writes from Miami: 

 State Department officials have quietly raised objections to El Salvador's gang-fighting efforts in Haiti — even as President Trump has offered his full support, according to diplomatic notes and informed sources.

 El Salvador issued a formal rebuke yesterday that questioned the "credibility" of the top U.S. diplomat in Haiti. Why it matters: The controversy exposes the tension between Trump's MAGA foreign policy objectives and the professional diplomatic establishment in the State Department.

 "There is a class of bureaucrats who don't want to see the change in the Western Hemisphere that POTUS wants," a U.S. official told Axios. Keep reading . 

 
 
