 8. 🌉 1 for the road: $100 million Airbnb gift 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Brian Chesky speaks yesterday at San Francisco's Conservatory of Flowers. Photo: Airbnb Brian Chesky , Airbnb co-founder and CEO, is donating $100 million to the San Francisco Recreation and Parks Department — the largest-ever donation to the city by an individual, Axios San Francisco's Nadia Lopez writes. 

 Chesky's donation is more than a third of the department's proposed spending for next year. Between the lines: San Francisco Mayor Daniel Lurie, who appeared with Chesky for yesterday's announcement, has increasingly sought private funding for initiatives addressing homelessness, public safety and the city's economic recovery.

 Chesky, whose global company was founded in San Francisco nearly two decades ago, serves on a council of business leaders advising the mayor on economic issues. Read the announcement ... Share this story . 

 
 
